refused[P2G8001]: `eval STRING` builds Perl source at run time, and Go has no
    compiler at run time
   --> logwatch.pl:143:19
    |
143 |     my $ok = eval "$threshold_expr";
    |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = not converted: this call site raises a panic carrying the original Perl
                     text
    = try: if the expressions come from a config file, embed an expression
           evaluator such as github.com/expr-lang/expr and pass the values as
           its environment; if there are only a handful of known expressions,
           replace them with named functions and dispatch on the name
    = learn: compile-time-mindset   (perl2golang explain compile-time-mindset)
    = learn: panic-and-recover   (perl2golang explain panic-and-recover)
